# Known invariant violations, measured by TestAdversarialInvariants.
#
# This file is a RATCHET, not an allow-list that silences a test:
#   - an invariant violated HERE and not listed is a NEW VIOLATION -> red
#   - an invariant listed here that now HOLDS is a STALE ENTRY     -> red
#   - each id below was predicted from the source at lane base (see the case's
#     `invariant` field and its detail line in the CI log for the measurement).
#
# Delete a line only when its case holds, so the fix is recorded with its gate.

# P0-C / ARCHITECTURE 34.3: the inherited keys are reported and never acted on.
# internal/commandline/options.go:250 resolves extensions.autoUpdate with a
# fallback of true and treats any configured value as an input;
# internal/server/settings_get.go:70 then reports it, and the frontend's
# autoUpdateExtensions() (upstream/public/scripts/extensions.js:1988-2010)
# drives POST /api/extensions/update from it.

# rule 26: an unparseable value is an OFF input; jsBoolean("maybe") is true.

# rule 27: a parseable config is rewritten on boot by mergeDefaults.
config.parseable-config-rewritten

# rule 24/27: a config that parses is not a licence to resolve a relative
# dataRoot against two different roots (internal/commandline/paths.go:155 uses
# the working directory, :175 uses the server directory).
boot.foreign-cwd-relative-data-root

# rule 24: flock.Lock() has no bounded acquisition (internal/configinit/config.go:169,
# internal/startup/*.go lock helpers), so a held lock blocks the second process.
boot.data-startup-lock-held

# rule 24/33: the pinned ten-second legacy warning is spent in silence before any
# output, and main prints nothing until app.Start returns
# (internal/startup/user_data_migration.go:40).
boot.legacy-migration-cost

# rule 9/22: with no tokenizer tree the route answers 200 with a Guesstimate
# count instead of failing loudly (internal/server/tokenizers.go:363-372).
boot.missing-tokenizers

# rule 29/30: the wire client advertises accept-encoding gzip/deflate/br and
# never decompresses (internal/outbound/raw.go has no compress/* import).

# rule 29: 3xx is returned to the caller as the provider's answer; no Location
# handling exists in internal/outbound/raw.go.

# rule 29: HTTPS_PROXY is never read (no ProxyFromEnvironment anywhere) even
# though the pinned config carries requestProxy.enabled/url/bypass, which
# internal/commandline/options.go:231-233 parses and nothing consumes.
transport.proxy-connect-ignored

# rule 35/12: a credential containing CR/LF is written verbatim by
# internal/outbound/raw.go:149-151, so it forges a request header.
